.TH EUCLID-CLI-EMO-DELETE-ALERT-RULE 1 "October 2026" "euclid-cli 2.1.3" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-emo-delete-alert-rule \- delete a threshold alert rule, clearing what it raised
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli emo delete-alert-rule
.B \-\-rule\-id
.I ID
.SH DESCRIPTION
Deletes a rule and the state of every series it judged.
.PP
Each series not OK is cleared first, and published as
.I emo.alert.cleared
with reason
.IR rule-deleted .
A subscriber that was told CRITICAL is told it is over, rather than
waiting on a rule that no longer exists.
.PP
The rule's history stays, and expires with the rest of it after
.I euclid.modules.emo.alert.history-retention
days. To stop a rule for a while without losing it, disable it with
.BR euclid-cli-emo-update-alert-rule (1)
instead.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-rule\-id " " \fIID\fR
The rule to delete. Required.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The rule was deleted.
.TP
.B 1
The caller was not authenticated or is not an administrator, or there is
no rule of that id (HTTP 404).
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli emo delete-alert-rule --rule-id system-cpu-per-host
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-emo (1),
.BR euclid-cli-emo-update-alert-rule (1),
.BR euclid-cli-emo-list-alert-history (1)
